{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"despiteous-observant-dikdik","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Surface\nGitHub Actions, repo navapbc/rebar, workflow **Terraform Drift** (scheduled), job `plan`.\n\n## Signature\n`terraform init` succeeds configuring the s3 backend, then fails:\n```\nError: Unsupported Terraform Core version\n  required_version = \">= 1.11\"\nThis configuration does not support Terraform version 1.10.5.\n```\nThe runner/setup provisions Terraform **1.10.5**, but the config requires **>= 1.11**. The workflow cannot reach the drift `plan` at all — drift detection is blind while broken.\n\n## First/last seen in-window\nRun 33297247070 @ 2026-08-30T06:35Z (scheduled). Fails every scheduled run (deterministic version mismatch, not transient).\n\n## Dedup\nNo existing ticket found (searched \"terraform drift / unsupported core version / setup-terraform\"). Distinct from the last sweep's noted \"9350 drift\" item (that is a drift-content blocker, not a Core-version init failure). New signature.\n\n## Severity: P3\nMonitoring-only workflow; no user/merge/production impact. But it is a hard, deterministic failure — infra drift goes undetected until the Terraform version pin (setup-terraform) is bumped to satisfy `>= 1.11` (or the constraint relaxed).\n\n## Provenance\nPeriodic ops-error sweep (window 2026-08-29T10:00 → 2026-08-30T17:36 PDT). Triage only — not fixed.","id":"d227-7fa6-41ca-44cd","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"[terraform-drift] Terraform Drift workflow red: runner Terraform 1.10.5 does not satisfy required_version \">= 1.11\" (init fails before plan)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788137470530365974,"uuid":"b16a5baf-d381-49da-bca2-5a0f3f4fac88"}